 "Notes": [
  "Stone pieces cost iron for now: granite needs stone mining, which waits for learned mining skills. Switch their Cost to Granite then.",
  "Plot tiers take their price, storage and lockdowns from ServUO's customisable foundation of the same size (the 24x24 tier from its 23x23 keep). Storage and lockdowns aren't used yet.",
  "Blueprints are ServUO's classic houses, kept for the planned 'stamp a classic house' feature (BuildingDesign.md)."
 ],
 "PiecesText": {
  "Frame": "A piece is laid out in its own frame: X along its length, Z across, Y up from its level's floor line, metres. A Tile piece covers X 0..W*1.25 and Z 0..D*1.25 (W x D tiles); an Edge piece runs along a tile edge from X 0 to W*1.25 at Z 0. Rotation turns it a quarter at a time about its middle.",
  "Parts": "Kit prefabs placed in that frame (At: x, y, z; Yaw: degrees). Every part keeps its prefab's own colliders.",
  "Slot": "What a piece takes up, so two can't overlap: Floor (a tile's floor), Volume (a tile's space: stairs, roof slopes), Wall and Base (an edge; Base is below ground), Ridge (the top of an edge, for ridge caps).",
  "Levels": "Ground: level 0 only. Storeys: 0 to Storeys-1. Building: 0 to Storeys (floors, low walls and railings make a roof terrace). Roof: 1 to Storeys+RoofLevels-1.",
  "Paint": "Wall pieces take the house's wall style, Roof pieces its roof style (Styles / RoofStyles: material swaps of the kit's atlas).",
  "Door": "The part's door leaf opens with E like the world's doors; on a private house only the owner and friends can open it.",
  "Cost": "Materials taken from the builder's backpack (Crafting's resource equivalents apply: logs pay for boards). Removing a piece gives RefundShare of them back."
 }
